{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>This is the thing that YHWH has commanded.</b> In His saying: וּבַבֹּקֶר תִּשְׂבְּעוּ לֶחֶם (\"and in the morning you shall be filled with bread\")." "<b>Let every man gather of it.</b> Each one according to his desire, whether one gathers much or one gathers little." "<b>Every man according to his eating, an omer per head, according to the number of your persons — each man for those in his tent you shall take.</b> For no matter how you gather, whether you gather much or whether you gather little, it will in any case turn out that what is gathered provides sustenance for each one according to his eating — satisfying the one accustomed to eating much, while not giving more food than is proper to the one accustomed to eating little. And what is gathered, whether by the one who gathers much or by the one who gathers little, will be an omer per head — no less and no more. And the one who gathers for all the members of his household will gather an omer for each one, corresponding to the total number of persons in his tent."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:50.573934273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}